Steps :
> mkdir manggo-api
> cd manggo-api/

> npm init
	- description: APIs for MangGo App
	- entry point: (index.js) app.js
	- author: Adit
	- the rests yes

> git init
> copy .gitignore from other api project


> npm install --save express

Cors handler (express middleware) :
- npm install --save cors

For Logger, use Pino (instead of morgan) :
- npm install --save pino pino-http
- npm install --save-dev pino-pretty

For input validations :
- npm install --save express-validator
	detail docs of validation: https://github.com/validatorjs/validator.js/blob/master/README.md

Install Prisma :
	- npm install prisma@6 --save-dev
	- npm install --save @prisma/client@6

Setup schema.prisma file including DB-name within .env file, then:
	- npx prisma migrate dev --name init


Cloudinary Setup (Cloud-based image service):
	- npm install --save cloudinary



============================================
[Concepts]

Express - Prisma - DB (SQLite)

ExpressJs is used because the character of this app as the channel to core system, in this case AI system, where ExpressJs (NodeJs) do async style naturally.

Choosing SQL-based DB rather than document because of natural character of this app when growing bigger. The data most likely will be used for statistics/analytics or even billing, which is more natural using relational DB rather than unstructured ones.

Using Prisma as an abstraction layer of SQL-based DB, will ease migration to more enterprise grade DB, like PostgreSQL, at later time.


Express - Pollination AI API
Express - Cloudinary (Cloud Image service)



Data structure:

model ImageGenerationSession {
	id        String   @id @default(cuid())
	sessionId String   @unique

	contents  ImageGenerationContent[]

	createdAt DateTime @default(now())
	updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

	@@index([sessionId])
}

model ImageGenerationContent {
	id        		String @id @default(cuid())
	promptId  		String
	prompt    		String
	style     		String?
	enhancedPrompt 	String?

	imageUrl  		String?	// Cloudinary URL
	status    		String	// pending / processing / success / failed
	stage 			String? // request_received / generating_image / uploading_image / done
	error 			String? // (flexible JSON string)

	provider  		String?	// provider AI
	meta      		String?	// meta data AI (flexible JSON string)

	sessionId 		String
	session   		ImageGenerationSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id])

	createdAt 		DateTime @default(now())
}


