Sample error data:
	error: {
		ai: '',
		storage: 'failed to upload image'
	}


In order to give better UX for meaningful loading states at FE (10-30s is normal), here are the status to set:

Status:
	pending - request_received ("Pending request"):
		user submit, backend set "pending" state.

	processing:
		generating_image ("Generating AI image"): request pass to AI to generate image
		uploading_image ("Uploading image"): after image returned from AI, upload image to Cloudinary

	success - done: if AI and cloudinary upload success, set success.

	failed - done: if one of AI or cloudinary upload failed, set failed and set error for reason.



Samples to do polling at FE:

setInterval(async () => {
	const res = await fetch(`/api/image/${id}`)
	const data = await res.json()

	if (data.status === "success") {
		stopPolling()
	}
}, 2000)

async function checkStatus(id) {
	const res = await fetch(`/api/image/${id}`)
	const data = await res.json()

	if (data.status === "pending") {
		setTimeout(() => checkStatus(id), 2000)
	}

	if (data.status === "success") {
		console.log("done", data.imageUrl)
	}

	if (data.status === "failed") {
		console.log("error", data.error)
	}
}


===========================================
[To Pollinations AI API]

API GET IMAGE:
	https://gen.pollinations.ai/image/${encodedPrompt}?model=flux
	headers: {
		Authorization: 'Bearer YOUR_SECRET_TOKEN'
	}

return image file.


sample error:

{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "message": "Model 'zimage' is not allowed for this API key",
    "code": "FORBIDDEN",
    "timestamp": "2026-06-06T13:16:27.778Z"
  },
  "status": 403
}




